# gltron

A 3D lightcycle game, originally by Andreas Umbach (1999). This fork, maintained
by Bill Six (billsix@gmail.com), keeps gltron running on modern systems and uses
it as a **teaching artifact for graphics concepts** — the fixed-function OpenGL
pipeline is preserved on purpose.

## Status

- Ported SDL 1.2 → SDL2 → **SDL3**; audio via **SDL3_sound**; scripting via system
  **Lua 5.4**; linear algebra via vendored **HandmadeMath**. Written in **C11**.
- Runs on Linux and Windows; macOS builds, but the SDL3 path hasn't been retested.
- Build system: **CMake ≥ 3.21** (Ninja recommended), out-of-tree only.

## Building

Dependencies: SDL3 (≥ 3.2), SDL3_sound, OpenGL, GLEW, libpng, zlib, Lua 5.4.

```sh
cmake -S . -B build -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
cmake --build build
```

(See `INSTALL` for the full dependency and option list.)

### Containerized dev build (Fedora / podman)

```sh
make -f Makefile.docker image    # build the image; compiles gltron + runs ctest
make -f Makefile.docker shell    # dev shell (X11/Wayland + audio forwarded)
make -f Makefile.docker build    # re-run the CMake build against the source tree
make -f Makefile.docker appimage # build a Linux AppImage into ./out/
```

## Runtime config

User config lives at `~/.gltronrc` (and sometimes a `~/.gltron/` directory).
Delete them to reset to defaults.

## Soundtrack

`gltron.it` — 'Revenge of Cats' by Peter Hajba <skaven@remedy.fi>.

